{
	// Cloudflare Workers static-assets config for the docs site.
	// The Pages "Connect to Git" flow now provisions a Worker (not a classic
	// Pages project), so it runs `npx wrangler deploy`, which reads this file
	// at the repo root. This is an assets-only Worker (no `main` script): it
	// just serves the static Astro build.
	//
	// Build settings in the Cloudflare dashboard:
	//   Root directory: /  (this file must sit in it — see the name note below)
	//   Build command:  npm run build -w @antiphony/docs
	//   Deploy command: npx wrangler deploy
	//   (this file's `assets.directory` is what gets uploaded)
	//
	// ## `name` MUST equal the Worker in the dashboard
	//
	// It is `antiphony-docs` there, and this said `antiphony` from the day the
	// file was added — a Worker by that name has never existed on the account.
	// Workers Builds checks the two before it builds and FAILS the build when
	// they disagree, which is what the docs site's builds were dying on:
	//
	//   "the Worker name in the Cloudflare dashboard must match the `name` in
	//    the Wrangler configuration file in the specified root directory, or
	//    the build will fail"
	//   — developers.cloudflare.com/workers/ci-cd/builds/
	//
	// Nothing about the build or the assets was wrong, which is why it read as
	// mysterious: `npm run build -w @antiphony/docs` and `wrangler deploy
	// --dry-run` both pass locally on a cold clone. Renaming the Worker in the
	// dashboard instead of this field would work equally well, but this field
	// is the half that is in version control.
	//
	// The repo has TWO Workers. This one is the docs site; core-api has its own
	// config at `apps/core-api/wrangler.jsonc`, because a wrangler config
	// describes exactly one Worker and the dashboard build for THIS one runs a
	// bare `npx wrangler deploy` at the repo root — so it must keep finding
	// this file and nothing else. Deploy the API explicitly:
	//
	//     npx wrangler deploy -c apps/core-api/wrangler.jsonc
	//
	// Nothing in this file touches core-api. core-api itself is no longer
	// mid-migration: it has served api.antiphony.dev from Workers + Neon since
	// 2026-08-17. See specs/cloudflare-migration.md.
	"$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
	"name": "antiphony-docs",
	"compatibility_date": "2025-01-01",
	"assets": {
		"directory": "./apps/docs/dist",

		// Astro builds a styled 404 page; without this the assets runtime
		// answers an unmatched path with a bare plain-text 404 and that file is
		// never served. Starlight's 404 carries the site nav, so a mistyped or
		// moved docs URL lands somewhere useful instead of a dead end.
		"not_found_handling": "404-page"
	}
}
